WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.418
Module 8: interpreting Mosaic data.

00:00:02.418 --> 00:00:06.287
This is the module the rest
of the course builds toward.

00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:10.570
You'll learn to read every number
and chart the tools produce,

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.923
say how confident you are and
why, tell real change from noise,

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:19.966
and turn a sixty-slide report into
three to five findings you can defend.

00:00:19.966 --> 00:00:23.144
It takes about three
hours, so take your time.

00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:26.030
Anyone can generate a Mosaic report.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.628
It takes a button press.

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:32.356
What a client pays a practitioner
for is knowing what the report means,

00:00:32.356 --> 00:00:33.688
and what it doesn't.

00:00:33.688 --> 00:00:37.150
Three questions sit under
everything in this module.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.747
What does this number actually measure?

00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:45.207
A fifty-two on a tile, a fifty-second
percentile and a slider average of fifty-two

00:00:45.207 --> 00:00:47.737
are three completely different things.

00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:49.002
How sure can we be?

00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:53.863
A score from four hundred people and
a score from eight deserve different

00:00:53.863 --> 00:00:54.596
confidence.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:55.395
And so what?

00:00:55.395 --> 00:00:59.656
A finding earns its place when it
helps someone make a decision.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:04.290
Open any Mosaic report and you'll
meet four kinds of number.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:08.276
First, the item mean: the
average answer to one statement.

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:11.849
In the Culture Mosaic that's
on a one-to-five scale,

00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:15.079
and in the Leadership
Mosaic it's one to seven.

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:17.690
Second, the zero-to-one-hundred score.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:22.019
It takes an average and places
it on a common ruler, so a tile,

00:01:22.019 --> 00:01:25.593
a dimension or a domain can
be compared at a glance.

00:01:25.593 --> 00:01:27.105
Third, the percentile.

00:01:27.105 --> 00:01:31.365
A percentile doesn't tell you
how well people rated something.

00:01:31.365 --> 00:01:36.176
It tells you where that rating ranks
against a comparison group: other

00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:41.536
organizations for the Culture Mosaic,
other leaders for the Leadership Mosaic.

00:01:41.536 --> 00:01:44.078
And fourth, Typical Scores of Others,

00:01:44.078 --> 00:01:47.514
a reference point from that
same comparison group.

00:01:47.514 --> 00:01:51.706
Most interpretation errors start
with mixing up two of these.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.464
This table puts the measures for each
tool side by side: the answer scale,

00:01:57.464 --> 00:02:00.879
how the zero-to-one-hundred
score is calculated,

00:02:00.879 --> 00:02:05.076
what the percentile compares
against, what "typical" means,

00:02:05.076 --> 00:02:07.068
and how confidence is shown.

00:02:07.068 --> 00:02:10.198
It's in your job aids
too, so keep it handy.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.725
The Culture Mosaic uses
a one-to-five scale,

00:02:13.725 --> 00:02:16.750
and the Leadership Mosaic
uses one to seven.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.562
The words at each end are the same,
but the numbers aren't comparable.

00:02:21.562 --> 00:02:25.756
A four on the Culture Mosaic is
three-quarters of the way up.

00:02:25.756 --> 00:02:29.606
A four on the Leadership Mosaic
is exactly the midpoint.

00:02:29.606 --> 00:02:34.350
So never compare a Culture Mosaic
mean with a Leadership Mosaic mean.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:39.437
And in the Leadership Mosaic, a skipped
answer is left out of the average,

00:02:39.437 --> 00:02:40.950
never counted as zero.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:45.949
The zero-to-one-hundred score is
the mean placed on a common ruler,

00:02:45.949 --> 00:02:50.097
with the bottom of the scale at
zero and the top at a hundred.

00:02:50.097 --> 00:02:53.643
On the Culture Mosaic, a
mean of three becomes fifty.

00:02:53.643 --> 00:02:57.322
On the Leadership Mosaic, a
mean of four becomes fifty.

00:02:57.322 --> 00:03:02.608
For example, others rated Jordan Reyes
four point six on Adapt, which is sixty,

00:03:02.608 --> 00:03:06.956
and Jordan rated themselves five
point nine, which is eighty-two.

00:03:06.956 --> 00:03:08.897
Two things this score is not.

00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:13.379
It's not the percentage of people
who agreed, and it's not a grade.

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:14.784
There's no pass mark.

00:03:14.784 --> 00:03:20.337
A sixty is simply sixty percent of the way
from the bottom of the scale to the top.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.473
A tile pools the answers to its items,

00:03:23.473 --> 00:03:26.946
and the two instruments
pool slightly differently.

00:03:26.946 --> 00:03:30.628
In the Culture Mosaic, every
response counts equally,

00:03:30.628 --> 00:03:34.796
which keeps leader-only items
from carrying outsized weight.

00:03:34.796 --> 00:03:39.451
Reverse-scored items are flipped
first, so higher is always better.

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:43.063
In the Leadership Mosaic,
every item counts equally.

00:03:43.063 --> 00:03:48.273
On the Culture Mosaic, a dimension is
the plain average of its three tiles.

00:03:48.273 --> 00:03:50.565
Northwind's Adapt is fifty-eight.

00:03:50.565 --> 00:03:55.150
You'll sometimes see an item that
looks out of line with its tile.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.554
That's normal, and it's
why the item pages exist.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:03.090
A percentile answers one question:
out of the comparison group,

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.942
what share scored below this?

00:04:04.942 --> 00:04:09.986
In the Culture Mosaic, your organization's
average on an item is ranked against

00:04:09.986 --> 00:04:12.732
other organizations'
averages on that item.

00:04:12.732 --> 00:04:17.777
In the Leadership Mosaic, a leader is
ranked against other leaders in the pool,

00:04:17.777 --> 00:04:19.884
for the same item and rater type.

00:04:19.884 --> 00:04:22.439
Percentiles run from one to ninety-nine.

00:04:22.439 --> 00:04:27.611
Northwind's purpose item scored four point
four, at the eighty-eighth percentile,

00:04:27.611 --> 00:04:32.273
so Northwind rated it higher than
about eighty-eight percent of benchmark

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:33.167
organizations.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:33.997
Two cautions.

00:04:33.997 --> 00:04:36.743
A low percentile can
sit on a decent score,

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:41.405
if most organizations rate that item
highly, so always read both numbers.

00:04:41.405 --> 00:04:44.981
And the comparison group is
the gothamCulture benchmark,

00:04:44.981 --> 00:04:47.152
not every organization everywhere.

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:51.303
Say "compared with organizations
in the gothamCulture benchmark",

00:04:51.303 --> 00:04:55.517
not "compared with the industry",
and don't describe what's in it.

00:04:56.033 --> 00:05:01.400
Both reports show "Typical Scores of
Others", but they mean different things.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:07.184
On the Culture Mosaic, it's a single marker:
the median of benchmark organizations'

00:05:07.184 --> 00:05:10.599
averages, so half scored
above it and half below.

00:05:10.599 --> 00:05:14.989
On the Leadership Mosaic, it's
a grey band: the pool's average,

00:05:14.989 --> 00:05:17.568
plus or minus one standard deviation.

00:05:17.568 --> 00:05:22.028
Inside the band is unremarkable,
and outside it is worth a look.

00:05:22.028 --> 00:05:23.979
And typical is not a target.

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:29.555
An organization above typical on Customer
may still have a Customer problem that

00:05:29.555 --> 00:05:31.227
matters to its strategy.

00:05:31.227 --> 00:05:35.060
One below typical may be
making a deliberate trade-off.

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:40.261
Reports turn numbers into tile sizes
and shading so patterns jump out.

00:05:40.261 --> 00:05:43.749
Know what the shading is
made of before you read it.

00:05:43.749 --> 00:05:47.303
On the Culture Mosaic diamond
and comparison heatmap,

00:05:47.303 --> 00:05:50.992
size and shade come from the
zero-to-one-hundred score.

00:05:50.992 --> 00:05:55.150
On item heatmaps and on Leadership
Mosaic comparison diamonds,

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.961
they come from percentiles.

00:05:56.961 --> 00:06:01.924
So watch out: a big tile on the Culture
Mosaic diamond means a high score,

00:06:01.924 --> 00:06:07.490
while a big tile on a Leadership Mosaic
comparison diamond means a high percentile.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:10.910
They look the same, but
they're different measures.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.040
Quick check on the
toolkit before we move on.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:14.979
It isn't scored.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:18.877
Every item row shows N,
how many people answered.

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:21.105
Look at it before anything else.

00:06:21.105 --> 00:06:25.142
Northwind's purpose item has
four hundred and ten answers,

00:06:25.142 --> 00:06:28.205
so one person more or
less wouldn't move it.

00:06:28.205 --> 00:06:33.008
Its leader-only items have fifty-eight,
still solid, but less stable.

00:06:33.008 --> 00:06:38.368
And a group of eight can swing ten points
between surveys just because of who

00:06:38.368 --> 00:06:39.690
happened to answer.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:43.310
Build a habit: when you
quote a number, quote its N.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.600
"Collaboration is forty-four across all
four hundred and twelve respondents"

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.549
carries its own credibility.

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:55.303
The methodology box shows invited,
responded, and response rate.

00:06:55.303 --> 00:07:00.374
Northwind: six hundred and forty invited,
four hundred and twelve responded,

00:07:00.374 --> 00:07:01.642
sixty-four percent.

00:07:01.642 --> 00:07:06.712
A high rate doesn't guarantee accuracy,
and a low one doesn't ruin a survey.

00:07:06.712 --> 00:07:11.916
Ask instead whether the people who didn't
answer would see things differently.

00:07:11.916 --> 00:07:16.787
If a whole site or shift barely
responded, its view is under-represented.

00:07:16.787 --> 00:07:22.391
And if the report says "Not tracked",
SurveyCraft didn't know how many were invited.

00:07:22.391 --> 00:07:23.726
Don't invent a rate.

00:07:23.726 --> 00:07:26.194
Say it's unknown, and lean more on N.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:32.711
Mosaic reports deliberately hide numbers
that could expose individuals or mislead.

00:07:32.711 --> 00:07:36.596
A report that won't generate
means too few responses.

00:07:36.596 --> 00:07:42.461
A group that's missing, or folded into
"Other", is below the minimum group size.

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:46.639
A dash in a heatmap cell means
fewer than three answered.

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:51.037
A dash in a 360 rater column
means that category was folded.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:54.922
No percentile means the
comparison pool is too small.

00:07:54.922 --> 00:07:59.760
And Culture Dig's "too few to score"
means fewer than ten stories.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:01.886
These rules aren't obstacles.

00:08:01.886 --> 00:08:05.258
They're the promise every
respondent was made.

00:08:05.258 --> 00:08:10.536
Never reconstruct a hidden number by
subtracting one group from another,

00:08:10.536 --> 00:08:13.982
and never present a group
the report rolled up.

00:08:14.467 --> 00:08:18.663
The report's own heatmap note
says it: small groups vary more,

00:08:18.663 --> 00:08:21.371
so expect more very high and low values.

00:08:21.371 --> 00:08:26.515
A group of eight that moves ten points
tells you much less than a group of a

00:08:26.515 --> 00:08:28.884
hundred and sixty that moves three.

00:08:28.884 --> 00:08:34.163
If a group is small, describe its result
as worth exploring, not as a finding.

00:08:34.667 --> 00:08:37.125
Let's walk the Culture Mosaic deck.

00:08:37.125 --> 00:08:39.793
The framework pages orient executives,

00:08:39.793 --> 00:08:45.060
and on Links to Performance you can
read the footnote aloud if you need to.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:50.257
The headline diamond shows all twelve
tile scores and the methodology box.

00:08:50.257 --> 00:08:54.541
Look at the overall shape, and
check the response rate first.

00:08:54.541 --> 00:08:58.895
The dimension and item pages show
which items drive each tile,

00:08:58.895 --> 00:09:01.002
with leader-only items marked.

00:09:01.002 --> 00:09:03.670
The item heatmaps show items by group,

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:07.954
so look for whole rows or columns
that are darker or lighter.

00:09:07.954 --> 00:09:11.325
One odd cell in a small
group is rarely a story.

00:09:11.325 --> 00:09:17.014
The comparison reports show a mini-mosaic
per group for each breakdown the client

00:09:17.014 --> 00:09:19.682
set up, plus Leader versus Non-Leader.

00:09:19.682 --> 00:09:24.317
The free-response pages give themes
tagged Many, Several or A few.

00:09:24.317 --> 00:09:28.250
Then the Psychological Safety
Index, any subscales, and,

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:33.166
if the client added their own questions,
"Your Questions" at the back.

00:09:33.166 --> 00:09:38.644
Ask whether the client's own questions
confirm or complicate what the standard

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:39.346
items say.

00:09:39.833 --> 00:09:44.077
Read the Culture Mosaic from
the top down, then back up.

00:09:44.077 --> 00:09:49.835
At dimension level, Northwind's Inspire
is strongest at sixty-six and Enable

00:09:49.835 --> 00:09:51.502
weakest at fifty-four.

00:09:51.502 --> 00:09:55.670
That's a start, but dimensions
average away the detail.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:10:01.883
At tile level, inside Inspire there's a
thirty-one-point spread between Purpose at

00:10:01.883 --> 00:10:04.687
eighty-two and Strategy at fifty-one.

00:10:04.687 --> 00:10:10.976
"People know why we exist, but not how
we're getting there" is far more useful than

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:12.719
"Inspire is sixty-six".

00:10:12.719 --> 00:10:15.446
At item level, inside Collaboration,

00:10:15.446 --> 00:10:21.508
the item about openly exploring disagreements
sits at the fourteenth percentile.

00:10:21.508 --> 00:10:24.615
That's a specific, discussable behaviour.

00:10:24.615 --> 00:10:25.827
Then go back up.

00:10:25.827 --> 00:10:28.782
Does the item story fit the tile story?

00:10:28.782 --> 00:10:31.434
Here it does: collaboration is low,

00:10:31.434 --> 00:10:36.284
and one reason is that disagreement
isn't worked through openly.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.507
Most Culture Mosaics include
a Leader Status comparison.

00:10:40.507 --> 00:10:45.936
At Northwind, leaders and non-leaders agree
on Purpose: eighty-six and eighty-one,

00:10:45.936 --> 00:10:47.062
a five-point gap.

00:10:47.062 --> 00:10:48.452
That's a shared view.

00:10:48.452 --> 00:10:53.550
But on Strategy and Empowered Teams,
leaders score twenty-five points higher.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:56.926
Leaders experience something
the frontline doesn't.

00:10:56.926 --> 00:11:00.567
That's one of the most useful
patterns in culture work,

00:11:00.567 --> 00:11:05.135
because leaders usually make decisions
based on their own experience.

00:11:05.135 --> 00:11:06.791
Don't decide who's right.

00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:10.498
Both views are data, and the
gap is a finding in itself.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.162
Read a heatmap in three passes.

00:11:13.162 --> 00:11:18.323
Rows first: which tiles are low
everywhere, and which only in some groups?

00:11:18.323 --> 00:11:22.159
Purpose is high in every
department, a shared strength.

00:11:22.159 --> 00:11:25.995
Collaboration is low in
Nursing and the Clinic Network,

00:11:25.995 --> 00:11:28.158
but not in Admin and Corporate.

00:11:28.158 --> 00:11:32.342
Columns next: which group is
consistently lighter or darker?

00:11:32.342 --> 00:11:36.178
The Clinic Network, mostly
the merged Lakeside clinics,

00:11:36.178 --> 00:11:39.247
is lowest on Change
Ready and Collaboration.

00:11:39.247 --> 00:11:42.107
That's the merger showing up in the data.

00:11:42.107 --> 00:11:43.013
Then check N.

00:11:43.013 --> 00:11:47.477
The "Other" column has twenty
people, so treat it as indicative.

00:11:47.477 --> 00:11:53.266
And never name, guess at, or work out the
scores of a department folded into Other.

00:11:53.767 --> 00:11:59.158
The Psychological Safety Index is
calculated from four Culture Mosaic items,

00:11:59.158 --> 00:12:03.131
rounded to a whole number that
picks one of five slides.

00:12:03.131 --> 00:12:07.316
Northwind scored two point nine
six, which rounds to three.

00:12:07.316 --> 00:12:13.062
Its slide says the level of psychological
safety is acceptable to attempt change,

00:12:13.062 --> 00:12:15.261
but presents a risk to success.

00:12:15.261 --> 00:12:18.383
Use it as a readiness
signal, not a verdict.

00:12:18.383 --> 00:12:21.717
The slide shows the level,
not the exact score.

00:12:21.717 --> 00:12:25.477
Northwind's two point nine
six is just over the line,

00:12:25.477 --> 00:12:30.939
at the cautious end of acceptable, so
don't read acceptable as a green light.

00:12:30.939 --> 00:12:32.003
And connect it.

00:12:32.003 --> 00:12:34.131
Northwind's low Collaboration,

00:12:34.131 --> 00:12:38.246
its low "speaking up" item at
the twenty-first percentile,

00:12:38.246 --> 00:12:41.367
and its safety index
all point the same way.

00:12:41.367 --> 00:12:45.411
That's convergent evidence,
stronger than any one number.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:51.489
Each standard open question gets an
AI-written summary page: how many responded,

00:12:51.489 --> 00:12:56.589
a short headline, and three or four
themes tagged Many, Several or A few.

00:12:56.589 --> 00:12:59.524
Group summaries follow, never with quotes.

00:12:59.524 --> 00:13:00.502
Use them well.

00:13:00.502 --> 00:13:06.301
Prevalence words are deliberately vague,
so don't convert "Many" into a percentage.

00:13:06.301 --> 00:13:11.680
Use themes to explain numbers: Northwind's
"cross-site coordination after the

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:16.152
merger" explains why Collaboration
is low in the Clinic Network.

00:13:16.152 --> 00:13:21.042
Look for themes the numbers don't
cover, like "staffing and workload".

00:13:21.042 --> 00:13:25.164
And if you ever see something
identifying, don't repeat it.

00:13:25.164 --> 00:13:27.330
Flag it to your Mosaic contact.

